  "generated_text": "1. Use the midpoint formula: \\(\\left( \\frac{x_1 + x_2}{2}, \\frac{y_1 + y_2}{2} \\right)\\).\n2. Let the other endpoint be \\((x, y)\\).\n3. According to the midpoint formula, we have:\n   \\[\n   \\frac{4 + x}{2} = 2 \\quad \\text{and} \\quad \\frac{3 + y}{2} = 9\n   \\]\n4. Solve for \\(x\\):\n   \\[\n   4 + x = 4 \\implies x = 0\n   \\]\n5. Solve for \\(y\\):\n   \\[\n   3 + y = 18 \\implies y = 15\n   \\]\n6. The coordinates of the other endpoint are \\((0, 15)\\).\n7. The sum of the coordinates of the other endpoint is:\n   \\[\n   0 + 15 = 15\n   \\]\n\nTherefore, the sum of the coordinates of the other endpoint is \\(\\boxed{15}\\).",
  "grade": {
